      "replayedSourceContext": "Official action/result:\n\nMotion by Vice Mayor/Vice President Niederhofer, seconded by Mayor/President Kiesel, and carried unanimously, 5-0-0, adopting Minute Order No\n\nOfficial item context:\n\n/Director\nSullivan, and carried unanimously, 5-0-0, adopting Minute Order No. 2078, receiving and\naccepting the report on Fiscal Year 2025-26 Third Quarter Financial Update.\n\nPUBLIC HEARING\n\nFY 2026-27 AND FY 2027-28 PRELIMINARY BUDGET. MINUTE ORDER NO. 2079.\n\nFinance Director Cruz presented the staff report.\n\nMayor/President Kiesel opened a public hearing to hear and consider comments\nregarding the FY 2026-27 and FY 2027-28 Preliminary Budget.\n\nThe following people addressed the City Council/EMID Board of Directors via email:\n1. Michael Crocker;\n2. Yiming Luo;\n3. Evan Adams; and\n4. Frederic de Sauvage.\n\nYiming Luo addressed the City Council/EMID Board of Directors via teleconference.\n\nWithout objection from the City Council/EMID Board of Directors, Mayor/President Kiesel\nclosed the public hearing.\n\nMotion by Vice Mayor/Vice President Niederhofer, seconded by Mayor/President Kiesel,\nand carried unanimously, 5-0-0, adopting Minute Order No. 2079, receiving and accepting\nthe FY 2026-2027 and FY 2027-2028 Preliminary Budget and directing staff to proceed\nwith incorporating the terms from the preliminary budget into the final budget for FY 2026-\n2027 and FY 2027-2028 to be considered for adoption by the City Council/EMID Board\nof Directors on June 15, 2026.\n\nRESOLUTIONS FOR ADOPTION\n\nAMENDED AND RESTATED CITY/DISTRICT MANAGER STEFAN CHATWIN’S\nEMPLOYMENT AGREEMENT. CITY RESOLUTION NO. 2026-057. EMID\nRESOLUTION NO. 3852.\n\nCity Attorney/District Legal Counsel Stock presented the staff report.\n\nDiscussion ensued.\n\nMotion by Councilmember/Director Jimenez, seconded by Vice Mayor/Vice President\nNiderhofer, and carried unanimously, 5-0-0, adopting City Resolution No. 2026-057, “A\nResolution of the City Council of the City of Foster City Approving the Amended and\nRestated City Manager Stefan Chatwin’s Employment Agreement,” and EMID Resolution\nNo. 3852, “A Resolution of the Board of Directors of the Estero Municipal Improvement\nDistrict Approving the Amended and Restated District Manager Stefan Chatwin’s\nEmployment Agreement.”\n\nCOMMUNICATIONS\n\nCITY/DISTRICT WARRANT OF DEMANDS. NO ACTION TAKEN.\n\nCity/District Warrants of Demands were processed via ACH on May 5, 2026, and\nWarrants of Demands were Processed and Issued on May 14, 2026.\n\nCITY/DISTRICT MANAGER REPORTS, COUNCIL/BOARD STATEMENTS AND\nREQUESTS, AND COUNCIL LIAISON REPORTS\n\nActing City/District Manager Subhashini, on behalf of City/District Manager Chatwin,\nthanked the City Council/EMID Board of Directors for their consideration and approval of\nthe Foster City Police Officers Association (FCPOA) Memorandum of Understanding\n(MOU), and thanked the FCPOA and the City’s Human Resources staff for their efforts\nthroughout the process.\n\nCouncilmember/Director Sullivan thanked the Police Department for their enforcement\nagainst unlawful use of electric motorcycles and electric scooters. He stated he attended\nBowditch Middle School’s Ribbon Cutting event for their new Gym and Academic Core\nfacilities on May 20. O"
